::ENG3_U02_L01_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The gate hung open, but the path beyond it was covered with leaves no one had disturbed. Which literary element most clearly adds a layer of meaning? {
=The unused path as a symbol of neglected possibility#Correct. The path suggests an opportunity that has not been taken.
~The leaves as proof that the season is summer#The leaves do not prove summer and the meaning is deeper than season.
~The gate as a simple object with no meaning#The gate and path create symbolic meaning.
~The path as evidence that many people visit#The passage says the leaves are undisturbed, so this is inaccurate.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: Nella folded the invitation twice before placing it under the loose floorboard. Which element most strongly suggests secrecy? {
~The invitation's color#The passage does not mention color.
=Nella hiding the invitation under the floorboard#Correct. The action shows secrecy and adds tension.
~The fact that the invitation is folded#Folding may matter, but hiding it is stronger evidence of secrecy.
~The name Nella#The name does not create secrecy by itself.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The portrait above the fireplace seemed to watch Ben as he crossed the room. Which term best describes the portrait's effect? {
~Flashback#The passage does not move into an earlier time.
~Dialogue#No one speaks in the passage.
=Personification#Correct. The portrait is described as if it can watch.
~Resolution#The passage does not resolve a conflict.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The orchard was full of blossoms, but every tree had a white ribbon tied around its trunk. How does the contrast add meaning? {
~It proves the orchard is unhealthy.#Blossoms suggest life, so this overstates the evidence.
~It makes the scene purely cheerful.#The ribbons complicate the cheerful blossoms.
~It removes all conflict from the passage.#The contrast creates tension rather than removing it.
=It creates a mixed mood by pairing beauty with a sign of warning or memory.#Correct. The contrast adds emotional complexity.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The hallway narrowed until Victor had to turn sideways, though the door ahead remained bright. Which element adds to the passage's style? {
~A broad open setting#The hallway is narrowing, not broad.
~A comic narrator#The passage does not signal humor.
=Claustrophobic setting details#Correct. The narrowing hallway creates pressure and tension.
~A complete lack of imagery#The passage uses visual and spatial imagery.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q06::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The letter smelled faintly of smoke, though its paper was clean. Which response best evaluates the sensory detail? {
~The smoke smell is random and cannot matter.#Sensory details often add meaning and mood.
=The smell of smoke adds unease because it suggests a hidden danger or past event.#Correct. This evaluates how the sensory detail adds meaning.
~The clean paper proves there is no conflict.#The smoke smell complicates the clean paper.
~The letter is only important because it has paper.#This is surface-level and weak.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q07::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: Whenever the mayor spoke, the cracked bell in the tower rang once by itself. Which element most affects the style? {
=The repeated strange sound of the bell#Correct. The sound creates a mysterious and uneasy style.
~The mayor's job title only#The title matters less than the repeated bell.
~The lack of any setting#There is a tower setting.
~The absence of all conflict#The strange bell suggests conflict or unease.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q08::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The snow covered every footprint except one set leading toward the locked chapel. Which explanation best evaluates setting? {
~The setting shows that many people recently visited the chapel.#Only one set of footprints remains.
=The snowy setting isolates the footprints, making the chapel feel mysterious.#Correct. The setting draws attention to the footprints and adds suspense.
~The setting proves the chapel is warm inside.#The passage does not support this.
~The setting removes mystery because snow explains everything.#The snow increases mystery.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q09::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: Ada kept polishing the same silver spoon while the argument continued around her. What does the repeated action most likely add? {
~It shows Ada is focused only on cleaning.#That is a surface reading and misses emotional meaning.
~It proves Ada agrees with everyone in the argument.#The passage does not show agreement.
=It suggests Ada's discomfort or need for control during conflict.#Correct. The repeated action adds a layer of character meaning.
~It creates a cheerful and relaxed mood.#The argument and repeated polishing suggest tension.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q10::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The lighthouse lamp was dark, but sailors still left flowers at its door. Which evaluation is strongest? {
~The lighthouse is only a building near water.#This identifies setting but not meaning.
~The flowers prove the sailors dislike the lighthouse.#Flowers usually suggest respect or memory.
~The dark lamp makes the lighthouse unimportant.#The flowers show it still matters.
=The lighthouse symbolizes memory because people honor it even after its light is gone.#Correct. This explains how the element adds meaning.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q11::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The classroom map still showed borders from a country that no longer existed. Which element most clearly adds historical weight? {
=The outdated map#Correct. The outdated map suggests history, change, and memory.
~The classroom only#The classroom is setting, but the map carries the deeper meaning.
~The absence of students#The passage does not mention students.
~The fact that maps use paper#This is not the meaningful element.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q12::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The violin case was empty, but Elena carried it to every rehearsal. Which meaning does the empty case most likely add? {
~It proves Elena dislikes music.#The rehearsal setting suggests she remains connected to music.
=It suggests loss or longing connected to music.#Correct. The empty case adds emotional meaning beyond the surface action.
~It shows the case is too heavy.#The passage does not mention weight.
~It creates a comic mood.#The detail is more serious than comic.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q13::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The town square clock had no hands, but people still met beneath it at noon. Which response best evaluates the clock? {
~The clock tells exact time.#It has no hands, so it cannot tell exact time.
~The clock is meaningless because it is broken.#People still gather beneath it, so it carries meaning.
=The clock symbolizes shared habit or community memory despite no longer working.#Correct. This explains the deeper meaning.
~The clock proves the town has no schedule.#People still meet at noon.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q14::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: Mina's new shoes clicked loudly on the marble floor, but she stepped softer each time someone looked up. Which character detail adds meaning? {
~The marble floor's color#The passage does not mention color.
=Mina changing how she walks when noticed#Correct. Her action suggests self-consciousness or caution.
~The existence of shoes#The shoes matter because of sound and behavior, not existence alone.
~The fact that people look up#This matters, but Mina's response adds the character layer.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q15::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The village planted roses around the burned courthouse. Which evaluation is strongest? {
~The roses are only decorations.#This misses the contrast with the burned courthouse.
~The courthouse is not important because roses are present.#The setting remains important.
=The roses add a layer of renewal by contrasting beauty with damage.#Correct. This evaluates how the element adds meaning.
~The burned courthouse creates a purely cheerful tone.#The damage complicates the tone.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q16::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The narrator describes the sea as "a locked blue door." Which literary element is most important? {
~Dialogue#No character is speaking to another character here.
~Plot resolution#The passage does not resolve the plot.
~Historical allusion#No historical reference is made.
=Metaphor#Correct. The sea is compared to a locked door without using like or as.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q17::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The old piano missed three keys, but Luc played around the gaps until the song sounded whole. How does the piano add meaning? {
=It symbolizes imperfection being worked into something complete.#Correct. The piano's missing keys and Luc's playing add a layer of resilience.
~It proves Luc cannot play music.#The song sounds whole, so this is inaccurate.
~It shows the piano is brand new.#The piano is old and missing keys.
~It removes any theme from the passage.#The piano supports a theme rather than removing it.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q18::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: Each time the judge asked a question, the candle beside her bent toward the open window. Which element creates a tense style? {
~A bright celebration#The passage is tense, not celebratory.
=The candle bending with each question#Correct. The repeated movement links the questioning to an uneasy atmosphere.
~A peaceful outdoor scene#The scene is indoors and tense.
~A complete lack of sensory detail#The candle and window are sensory details.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q19::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The narrator calls the garden "a library of seeds." What does this metaphor add? {
~It proves the garden contains bookshelves.#The metaphor is figurative, not literal.
~It makes the garden seem empty.#A library of seeds suggests stored life or knowledge.
=It suggests the garden preserves knowledge, memory, or future growth.#Correct. The metaphor adds layers beyond a literal garden.
~It removes meaning from the setting.#The metaphor adds meaning.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q20::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: During the victory parade, Jalen noticed one torn flag folded in a shop window. How does the torn flag add meaning? {
~It creates a simple celebration with no complexity.#The torn flag complicates the victory mood.
~It proves the parade is imaginary.#The passage does not support that.
~It shows that shops cannot display flags.#The passage does not make this claim.
=It adds a layer of cost or loss beneath the public celebration.#Correct. The torn flag complicates the mood and meaning.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q21::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The narrator repeats the word "almost" whenever describing the family's repaired home. Which effect does the repetition most likely create? {
=It suggests the repair is incomplete and emotionally uneasy.#Correct. Repeating "almost" adds a layer of incompleteness.
~It proves the home is fully perfect.#Almost means not fully complete.
~It removes uncertainty from the description.#The repetition creates uncertainty.
~It creates a comic style only.#The detail is more uneasy than comic.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q22::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The courtroom windows were painted shut, though sunlight pushed against the glass. Which evaluation is strongest? {
~The windows only show the time of day.#They also add symbolic meaning.
=The windows suggest blocked truth or freedom because light cannot fully enter.#Correct. This evaluates the symbolic effect.
~The sunlight proves there is no conflict.#The painted-shut windows create conflict.
~The windows are unrelated to style.#The window imagery shapes style and meaning.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q23::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The child carried an umbrella through the dry house, opening it only when adults began whispering. Which element adds a layer of meaning? {
~The weather outside#The passage is inside and dry.
~The umbrella as a simple rain tool only#The umbrella is used symbolically, not literally.
=The umbrella as a symbol of protection from tension#Correct. The child opens it during whispering, suggesting emotional protection.
~The absence of all conflict#Adult whispering suggests conflict or tension.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q24::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The narrator describes the city at dawn as "polished steel, cold and shining." How does this description affect style? {
~It creates a soft and playful style.#Cold steel suggests a harder style.
~It removes all imagery.#The phrase is vivid imagery.
~It proves the city is literally made of steel.#The description is figurative.
=It creates a precise, hard-edged style that makes the city feel impressive but distant.#Correct. This evaluates how the imagery affects style.
}

::ENG3_U02_L01_Q25::[MLA.ENG3.R.01] Passage: The family table had one empty chair, but everyone placed a hand on its back before sitting down. Which response best evaluates the chair? {
~The chair is only furniture.#This misses its emotional meaning.
~The chair proves the family dislikes sitting.#This is unsupported.
=The chair symbolizes absence and shared remembrance.#Correct. The repeated gesture gives the chair emotional meaning.
~The chair creates a purely humorous mood.#The action suggests seriousness and memory.
}
